/*!
\page page_stTpcRawData StTpcRawData

\brief Top-level container for raw TPC ADC data from all sectors in one event.

\ref StTpcRawData is the top-level container for raw ADC data from the STAR TPC for one event.
It organises data as <b>event → sector → padrow → pad → time-bin sequences</b> and serves as
the primary structure passed between the DAQ decoder, simulation embedder, and TPC cluster
finder. Two supporting classes, \ref StTpcDigitalSector and \c StDigitalPair, implement the
lower levels of this hierarchy.

\section sec_rawdata_hierarchy Class Hierarchy and Containment

\verbatim
StObject
└── StTpcRawData                      (event-level, 24 sector slots)
    └── StTpcDigitalSector            (one per sector; padrow × pad × sequences)
        └── StDigitalPadRow           std::vector<StDigitalTimeBins>
            └── StDigitalTimeBins     std::vector<StDigitalPair>
                └── StDigitalPair     contiguous ADC run for one pad
\endverbatim

\ref StTpcRawData is owned by the StEvent framework (accessible via <tt>StEvent::tpcRawData()</tt>).

\section sec_rawdata_digitalpair StDigitalPair

A contiguous run of ADC samples on one pad, starting at a given time bin.

\subsection subsec_dp_members Data Members
- <tt>UShort_t mTime</tt> — Starting time-bin index (0-based, range 0–511).
- <tt>StVectorADC mAdc</tt> — <tt>std::vector<Short_t></tt> of ADC samples for consecutive
  time bins. Each sample covers one 100-ns drift time bin.
- <tt>StVectorIDT mIdt</tt> — <tt>std::vector<UShort_t></tt> of MC truth track IDs (one per ADC
  sample); only populated for simulation.

\subsection subsec_dp_methods Key Methods
- <tt>void add(Short_t adc)</tt> — Appends one ADC sample (real data).
- <tt>void add(Short_t adc, Int_t idt)</tt> — Appends one ADC sample plus MC truth ID (simulation).
- <tt>Short_t* adc() const</tt> — Pointer to the first ADC sample.
- <tt>Bool_t isIdt() const</tt> — True when the MC truth ID array is populated.
- <tt>UShort_t* idt() const</tt> — Pointer to the MC truth ID array, or null.
- <tt>Int_t size() const</tt> — Number of ADC samples.
- <tt>UShort_t time() const</tt> — Starting time-bin index.

\section sec_rawdata_sector StTpcDigitalSector

Holds all raw ADC data for one TPC sector as a 3-D array
<tt>mData[padrow-1][pad-1]</tt> of \c StDigitalTimeBins.

\subsection subsec_ds_members Data Members
- <tt>StDigitalSector mData</tt> — 3-D ADC data: [padrow][pad][time-bin sequences].
- <tt>Int_t mSector</tt> — TPC sector number (1–24).
- <tt>StVecPads mPadList</tt> — Scratch buffer for <tt>getPadList()</tt>.
- <tt>StVecSequence mSequence</tt> — Scratch buffer for <tt>getSequences()</tt>.
- <tt>StVecIds mIds</tt> — Scratch buffer for MC truth ID queries.
- <tt>Int_t mNoRows</tt> — Number of padrows from <tt>St_tpcPadConfigC</tt>.

\subsection subsec_ds_methods Key Methods
- <tt>const StDigitalTimeBins* timeBinsOfRowAndPad(Int_t row, Int_t pad) const</tt> — Time-bin
  sequences for the given padrow and pad (both 1-based).
- <tt>Int_t getSequences(row, pad, nSeq, seq, Ids)</tt> — Returns \c StSequence objects for the
  cluster finder, plus MC truth ID pointer array.
- <tt>Int_t getPadList(Int_t row, UChar_t** padList)</tt> — List of active 1-based pad numbers.
- <tt>Int_t getTimeAdc(row, pad, Short_t ADCs[512], UShort_t IDTs[512])</tt> — Flat expansion,
  no ADC conversion.
- <tt>Int_t getTimeAdc(row, pad, UChar_t ADCs[512], UShort_t IDTs[512])</tt> — Flat expansion
  with 10→8 bit log compression.
- <tt>Int_t putTimeAdc(row, pad, Short_t* ADCs, UShort_t* IDTs=0)</tt> — Store with 10→8
  compression.
- <tt>Int_t putTimeAdc(row, pad, UChar_t* ADCs, UShort_t* IDTs=0)</tt> — Store with 8→10
  expansion.
- <tt>void assignTimeBins(row, pad, StDigitalTimeBins*)</tt> — Replace sequences (1-based,
  swap semantics).
- <tt>void clear()</tt> — Clear all sequences; preserve row/pad structure.
- <tt>Int_t cleanup()</tt> — Remove entries with < 7 samples and empty rows.
- <tt>StTpcDigitalSector& operator+=(StTpcDigitalSector&)</tt> — Merge ADC data.

\section sec_rawdata_top StTpcRawData

\subsection subsec_tr_members Data Members
- <tt>std::vector<StTpcDigitalSector*> mSectors</tt> — Per-sector raw ADC data; null entries
  indicate sectors with no data.

\subsection subsec_tr_methods Key Methods
- <tt>StTpcDigitalSector* GetSector(UInt_t sector)</tt> — Returns sector pointer for 1-based
  sector number, or null.
- <tt>void setSector(UInt_t sector, StTpcDigitalSector*)</tt> — Store sector (transfers
  ownership; deletes previous entry).
- <tt>Int_t getVecOfPixels(StVectPixel&, sector, row, padMin, padMax, tMin, tMax)</tt> — Fills
  a vector of \ref StTpcPixel objects from the specified ranges.
- <tt>void Clear(const Option_t*)</tt> — Releases and deletes all owned sector objects.
- <tt>StTpcRawData& operator+=(StTpcRawData&)</tt> — Merges data sector-by-sector.

\section sec_rawdata_adc ADC Compression Tables

Two look-up tables from <tt>StRoot/StDaqLib/TPC/trans_table.hh</tt>:
- <tt>log10to8_table[1024]</tt> — 10-bit linear → 8-bit log-compressed.
- <tt>log8to10_table[256]</tt> — 8-bit log-compressed → 10-bit linear.

\section sec_rawdata_ownership Object Ownership

\ref StTpcRawData owns all \ref StTpcDigitalSector objects; <tt>Clear()</tt> deletes them.
<b>Do not delete StTpcDigitalSector* pointers obtained from GetSector().</b>

\section sec_rawdata_usage Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StTpcRawData* rawData = event->tpcRawData();
if (!rawData) return;

for (UInt_t iSec = 1; iSec <= 24; ++iSec) {
    StTpcDigitalSector* sec = rawData->GetSector(iSec);
    if (!sec) continue;

    for (Int_t iRow = 1; iRow <= sec->numberOfRows(); ++iRow) {
        UChar_t* padList = nullptr;
        Int_t nPads = sec->getPadList(iRow, &padList);

        for (Int_t iPadIdx = 0; iPadIdx < nPads; ++iPadIdx) {
            Int_t iPad = padList[iPadIdx];
            Short_t  adcs[512] = {};
            UShort_t idts[512] = {};
            sec->getTimeAdc(iRow, iPad, adcs, idts);
            for (Int_t tb = 0; tb < 512; ++tb) {
                if (adcs[tb] > 0)
                    processPixel(iSec, iRow, iPad, tb, adcs[tb]);
            }
        }
    }
}
\endcode

\sa \ref page_stTpcPixel, \ref page_stTpcHit, \ref page_stTpcHitCollection
*/
